{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:11057907 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:11057907 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"11057907","source":"MED","pmid":"11057907","doi":"10.1016/s0092-8674(00)00126-4","title":"Activation of the IkappaB kinase complex by TRAF6 requires a dimeric ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme complex and a unique polyubiquitin chain.","authorString":"Deng L, Wang C, Spencer E, Yang L, Braun A, You J, Slaughter C, Pickart C, Chen ZJ.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Deng L","lastName":"Deng","firstName":"L","initials":"L","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular Biology, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas 75390, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang C","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"C","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Spencer E","lastName":"Spencer","firstName":"E","initials":"E"},{"fullName":"Yang L","lastName":"Yang","firstName":"L","initials":"L"},{"fullName":"Braun A","lastName":"Braun","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"You J","lastName":"You","firstName":"J","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Slaughter C","lastName":"Slaughter","firstName":"C","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Pickart C","lastName":"Pickart","firstName":"C","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Chen ZJ","lastName":"Chen","firstName":"Z J","initials":"ZJ"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["related_data","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"2","volume":"103","journalIssueId":1072005,"dateOfPublication":"2000 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2000,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Cell","title":"Cell","essn":"1097-4172","issn":"0092-8674","isoabbreviation":"Cell","nlmid":"0413066"},"printPublicationDate":"2000-10-01"},"pubYear":"2000","pageInfo":"351-361","abstractText":"TRAF6 is a signal transducer in the NF-kappaB pathway that activates IkappaB kinase (IKK) in response to proinflammatory cytokines. We have purified a heterodimeric protein complex that links TRAF6 to IKK activation. Peptide mass fingerprinting analysis reveals that this complex is composed of the ubiquitin conjugating enzyme Ubc13 and the Ubc-like protein Uev1A. We find that TRAF6, a RING domain protein, functions together with Ubc13/Uev1A to catalyze the synthesis of unique polyubiquitin chains linked through lysine-63 (K63) of ubiquitin. Blockade of this polyubiquitin chain synthesis, but not inhibition of the proteasome, prevents the activation of IKK by TRAF6. These results unveil a new regulatory function for ubiquitin, in which IKK is activated through the assembly of K63-linked polyubiquitin chains.","affiliation":"Department of Molecular Biology, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas 75390, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"GM 60372","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"GM 59203","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Hela Cells"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell-Free System"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Biopolymers","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ligases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IP","qualifierName":"isolation & purification"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ubiquitin-Conjugating Enzymes"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ubiquitin-Protein Ligases"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"TNF Receptor-Associated Factor 6"},{"majorTop